This product includes software developed by Avi Craimer and Matthew
Fairtlough.  It began as https://github.com/AviCraimer/lax-logic-in-lean;
the formula algebra, the Hilbert axiom schemes and the proof-checking
data structures (LaxLogic/PLLFormula.lean, PLLAxiom.lean, PLLProof.lean,
FormattingUtils.lean) originate there.

MATHEMATICAL ATTRIBUTION.  Results due to others are attributed in the
module docstring of the file that formalises them: Fairtlough and Mendler
for Propositional Lax Logic, Curry's problem and the completeness
theorems; Mendler for the timing interpretation; Iemhoff for G3iLL and
G4iLL; Fiorentini and Ferrari for the refutation calculi; Lindley and
Stark for the double-negation lifting; Liang and Miller for LJF.
Formalisations of a published result are the formaliser's expression of
someone else's mathematics, and are marked as such.

MACHINE ASSISTANCE.  A substantial part of this development was written
with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic), under human direction and
review.  This is disclosed rather than disclaimed, because in this
project it is checkable rather than a matter of trust: every claim in the
default build target is verified by the Lean kernel, and the axioms each
headline theorem depends on are pinned in Core/Audit.lean so that a
change to them fails the build.  Machine assistance does not enlarge what
is claimed; the kernel bounds it.

